WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.038
Why this check?

2
00:00:01.038 --> 00:00:03.900
Gate 3 maps attributes through sync.

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.431
Before a single AD user is synchronized
into a tenant that already has cloud

4
00:00:08.431 --> 00:00:11.092
accounts, the sync engine
has to decide which

5
00:00:11.092 --> 00:00:13.825
incoming object matches
which cloud account.

6
00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:18.155
Microsoft Learn's pages on configuring
Entra Connect for an existing

7
00:00:18.155 --> 00:00:21.962
tenant and on Set Entra Dir Sync
Feature explain the two joins.

8
00:00:21.962 --> 00:00:25.534
A soft match joins on
the primary SMTP address,

9
00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:29.199
and on the U P N when soft
match on U P N is turned on.

10
00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:31.575
A hard match joins on the source anchor.

11
00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:36.437
Either one, left open, lets an AD
object take over a cloud account.

12
00:00:36.437 --> 00:00:40.311
Learn's existing-tenant page
advises keeping soft match blocked,

13
00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:44.327
offers a feature to block cloud
object takeover through hard match,

14
00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:48.200
and says to turn each off only
while a matching procedure needs it.

15
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.091
So the question is simple:
are both blocks on,

16
00:00:51.091 --> 00:00:54.463
and if not, is there an
approved window that says why?

17
00:00:54.463 --> 00:00:58.460
The guide lists this as Gate 3's
optional match-blocking check.
